/// The 11-stage production pipeline named in the brief — deliberately
/// a separate dimension from `AlbumStatus` (the selection lifecycle
/// from Prompt 31: pending_selection → selection_in_progress →
/// design_pending → printing → completed). `AlbumStatus` answers "is
/// the client still picking photos, or has that closed"; this answers
/// "where is the physical/digital album itself in production" — a
/// finer-grained pipeline that only starts moving once `AlbumStatus`
/// reaches `design_pending`. Keeping them separate means a studio
/// process built around this detailed pipeline never has to
/// reinterpret the coarser selection-lifecycle enum other parts of the
/// codebase (Prompt 31) already depend on.
enum AlbumProductionStage {
  photos_selected
  designer_assigned
  design_started
  proof_uploaded
  client_review
  revision_requested
  approved
  sent_to_print
